# .env.example: the environment this course can use. Copy it and fill in what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env        # .env is gitignored; never commit it
#
# NOTHING here is required. The Lean lessons, exercises, C demos, the proof
# guard and Rocq all run with no secrets at all. See docs/setup.md, "Secrets
# and API keys".
#
# How it's loaded: mise.toml reads .env into every `mise run …` task, natively
# and in the dev containers (the repo is mounted there, so the same file works).
# Running `python3 tools/llm_prove.py` directly, without mise, does NOT read
# .env: export the variable in your shell instead.
#
# IMPORTANT: leave a line commented out unless you're setting a real value.
# Values in .env take precedence over your shell and over Codespaces secrets,
# and an empty `NAME=` line UNSETS the variable. A blank
# `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=` would hide the key you set somewhere else.

# --- Stage 9: tools/llm_prove.py (`mise run 3-lab:llm-prove`) -----------------
# Anthropic API key: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Optional. Every run costs money (the script prints the token bill).
# Alternatives: export it in your shell, add it as a Codespaces secret (you're
# prompted when you create the codespace), or use an `ant auth login` profile.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Note: Claude Code (`claude`) doesn't need this; it uses its own login. If this
# variable is in Claude Code's environment (e.g. with mise activated in your
# shell), Claude Code may use API billing instead of your subscription.
